    "created_at": "2017-05-15T16:08:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-15T16:08:20Z",
    "body": "Another note: when opening a new window with `noopener`, we currently follow all steps for creating a new window, including copying `sessionStorage` from the existing window into the new window. This seems undesirable as we want `noopener` to imply that the opened window is not an auxiliary browsing context (from my understanding).  I imagine that web developers would not expect a new window opened with `noopener` to get a copy of `sessionStorage` from the original window.\r\n\r\nThis is currently the behavior in both Chrome and Firefox (haven't tested any other browsers).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
